{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The only top-level data variable, `N`, is a context input used to size simulated generated quantities and is not scored by any likelihood statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program contains no model block sampling statements, no parameters requiring priors, and no protected observed data interface.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
}

generated quantities {
  // Simulate model configuration from prior model
  real<lower=0> lambda = abs(normal_rng(0, 6));
  real<lower=0, upper=1> theta = beta_rng(1, 1);

  // Simulate data from observational model
  array[N] int y = rep_array(0, N);
  for (n in 1:N)
    if (!bernoulli_rng(theta))
      y[n] = poisson_rng(lambda);
}

","data_safe_json":"{"N": 5}","protected_variables":[]}
